    <string name="cues_intro">Madsaz translates or identifies the cries of infants aged 0—3 months to help parents understand their baby better. The app recognises the five sounds of the Dunstan Baby Language (DBL): neh means hungry; owh means tired and starting to get sleepy; eh means the need to burp; eairh means wind (a bloated tummy), and heh means discomfort (for example, a wet diaper or nappy, being too hot or too cold, or something else)</string>
