    <string name="cue_neh_sol_1">Feed your baby</string>
    <string name="cue_neh_sol_2">Don’t interrupt your baby’s feeding time</string>
    <string name="cue_neh_sol_3">Don’t try to burp your baby in the middle of feed</string>
    <string name="cue_neh_sol_4">Let your baby feed for as long as they want, unless they make the “Eh” sound during the feed</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_1">Help your baby fall asleep</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_2">If your baby is windy or gassy, make sure they sleep in the correct position</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_3">Make sure your baby has been burped so that they can fall asleep more easily</string>
    <string name="cue_owh_sol_4">Rock your baby to sleep; it’s a wonderful time for bonding</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_1">Burp your baby</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_2">Be ready to burp your baby throughout the day, not only after feeds</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_3">If your baby makes the “Eh” sound before a feed, burp them first. Don’t feed a baby who needs to be burped</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_4">Don’t assume that a loud burp means the air bubbles have been removed; you will know when your baby stops making the “Eh” sound</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_5">If your baby is sleeping when you hear the "Eh" sound, try burping them first and then put them back to sleep to finish their nap</string>
    <string name="cue_eh_sol_6">When you swaddle a windy baby, wrap them snugly around the tummy, but leave their legs and arms free so they can move them when necessary</string>
    <string name="cue_eairh_sol_1">Use massage and wind-relieving holds. For example, cross your legs, lay your baby’s tummy down across your thigh and rock gently, applying light pressure with your knee to your baby’s lower tummy</string>
